# Project Curiosity

This is an engineering notebook, not a portfolio. Every page answers "how does Alex think?"

## Never

- Add neon, glassmorphism, SaaS gradients or flashy animation.
- Prioritise visuals over the story.
- Add generic portfolio sections (testimonials, skill bars, "hire me" banners).
- Add a dependency without a clear reason it beats the built-in option.

## Always

- Story before technology. Show the question before the solution.
- Preserve the editorial layout and prefer whitespace over decoration.
- Keep components small, reusable and typed. No `any`.
- Accessibility first: semantic HTML, visible focus, keyboard reachable, honour
  `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Animation should explain something, never entertain.

## Stack conventions

- Next.js App Router with `output: 'export'`. Every route must be statically renderable;
  no server actions, route handlers or runtime data fetching.
- Content lives in `content/` as MDX and is validated by `content-collections.ts`. Add
  fields to the Zod schema rather than reading frontmatter ad hoc.
- Styling is Tailwind v4 using the tokens in `src/styles/globals.css`. Use the semantic
  token names (`paper`, `ink`, `accent-rust`) rather than raw hex or default palette colours.
- Server Components by default. Add `'use client'` only where interactivity requires it.
- Imports use the `@/` alias for anything under `src/`.

## Writing

Follow `docs/02-project--spec/04_CONTENT_STYLE_GUIDE.md`: honest, curious, technical.
Use "I wondered if...", "I tried...", "This failed...", "I discovered...".
Never use "revolutionary" or "groundbreaking". Every experiment write-up must include
something that did not work.
